    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes: $3\\,816\\,547\\,290$.\n\nEach initial $k$-digit number is divisible by $k$.",
      "worked": "Yes. Arrange the cards as $3,8,1,6,5,4,7,2,9,0$. Each digit is used exactly once. The successive checks are\n$$\\begin{align*}38&=2\\times19\\\\381&=3\\times127\\\\3816&=4\\times954\\\\38165&=5\\times7633\\\\381654&=6\\times63609\\\\3816547&=7\\times545221\\\\38165472&=8\\times4770684\\\\381654729&=9\\times42406081\\\\3816547290&=10\\times381654729.\\end{align*}$$\nThus every required prefix has the stated divisibility.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
